  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "You are supplied with $500 \\mathrm{mL}$ each of $2 \\mathrm{N} \\mathrm{HCl}$ and $5 \\mathrm{N} \\mathrm{HCl}$. What is the maximum volume of 3M HCl that you can prepare using only these two solutions?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "FhTBK",
      "text": "$250 \\mathrm{mL}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Vm6ue",
      "text": "$500 \\mathrm{nL}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "0WKs7",
      "text": "$750 \\mathrm{mL}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Ybevz",
      "text": "$1000 \\mathrm{mL}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "As per given relation,\n$\\begin{array}{l}\nN_{1} V_{1}+N_{2} V_{2}=N\\left(V_{1}+V_{2}\\right) \\\\\nN_{1}=2 N_{2}=5 \\\\\nV_{1}=500 V_{2}=\\operatorname{say}-x\n\\end{array}$\nThus, $2 \\times 500+5 x=3(x+500)$ or $2 x=500^{\\circ}$\nie. $x=250$\nHence, maximum volume of\n$3 \\mathrm{M} \\mathrm{HCl}=500+250=750 \\mathrm{mL}$",
    "image": null
  },
